{%- comment -%}
  Oversized display word used as a typographic section marker.

  Decorative only. It repeats a word already present in the visible heading,
  so it is aria-hidden and nothing is lost by not announcing it. It sits at
  very low contrast on purpose — it is texture, not text to be read, and it
  must never compete with the copy in front of it.

  The parent must be position: relative and clip its overflow, or a word
  wider than the viewport will widen the page.

  Accepts: word {String}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if word != blank -%}
  <span class="ghost-word" aria-hidden="true">{{ word }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
